return {
["16:00"]={"“Think of me to-morrow, my dear Emma, about \003four o’clock\004,” was Mrs. Weston’s parting injunction; spoken with some anxiety, and meant only for her.","Emma","Jane Austen"},
["16:01"]={"Light is coming in through the curtains. Suddenly the digits on the clock radio look like a year. \0031601\004. I woke up a bit early, don’t have to be born for another 400 years.","101 Reykjavik","Hallgrímur Helgason"},
["16:02"]={"I’d just looked up at the clock, to make sure time wasn’t getting away from me, when I heard the shot. It was \003two minutes after four\004. I didn’t know what to do.","Southern Ghost","Carolyn G. Hart"},
["16:03"]={"Rose Rennick arrived \003a few minutes after four\004, accompanied by two small dogs and wearing an outrageously large hat.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["16:04"]={"At \003four past four\004 he was aware of a rustling train’s rush down the steps, and now was like a man with his neck on the block, awaiting the axe.","The Lord of the Sea","M.P. Shiel"},
["16:05"]={"IT was exactly \003five minutes past four\004 as Mr. Robert Audley stepped out upon the platform at Shoreditch, and waited placidly … it took a long while to make matters agreeable to all claimants, and even the barrister’s seraphic indifference to mundane affairs nearly gave way.","Lady Audley’s Secret","Mary Elizabeth Braddon"},
["16:06"]={"At \003six minutes after four\004, Benny’s Cadillac pulled up in front of Mr. Botelia’s store, and Benny’s mother stepped out of the car with Penelope, who was gnawing on the tip of an ice cream cone.","Follow Me: A Novel","Joanna Scott"},
["16:07"]={"At \003seven minutes past four\004 radio silence was broken with the five words, “Shoplifter apprehended, repeat Shoplifter apprehended.”","First Among Equals","Jeffrey Archer"},
["16:08"]={"It was \003eight minutes after four\004. I still don’t have a plan. Maybe the guys in the Nova, maybe they had a plan.","The Monkey’s Raincoat","Robert Crais"},
["16:09"]={"“You can take the 3:17 to Peterborough, where you’ll have to change and catch the \0034:09\004 for Doncaster, then change again. You’ll arrive in Hull at 6:32.”","Dougie Mortimer’s Right Arm","Jeffrey Archer"},
["16:10"]={"This Saturday he had left the greetings to Father Martin, but at \003ten past four\004 he thought it would be courteous to put in an appearance.","Death in Holy Orders","P.D. James"},
["16:11"]={"\0034:11 P.M.\004 Thurs. A Huey helicopter flies east overhead as the last of the U.S. Marines make ready to leave the beach; a buzzard dangles in the thermals closer over the town.","Seek","Denis Johnson"},
["16:12"]={"At precisely \003twelve minutes after four\004 a body of cavalry rode into the square, four abreast, clearing a way for the funeral cortege.","The Empty Mirror","J. Sydney Jones"},
["16:13"]={"But at precisely \0034:13 pm\004, the fifty thousand spectators saw the totally unexpected happen, before their very eyes. From the most crowded section of the southern grandstand, an apparition suddenly emerged.","Aunt Julia and the Scriptwriter","Mario Vargas Llosa"},
["16:14"]={"Then at \0034:14 pm\004 on March 12 I moved behind zinc-zirconium-not-to-be-revealed-compounds protecting me in this hill, and God have mercy but the struggle is just exchanged for the next one, which is exhausting me further as I say, to separate the true from the false.","Already Dead","Denis Johnson"},
["16:15"]={"It is only a \003quarter past four\004, (shewing his watch) and you are not now in Bath. No theatre, no rooms to prepare for. Half an hour at Northanger must be enough.","Northanger Abbey","Jane Austen"},
["16:16"]={"\0034:16 pm\004. The terrace outside the bar is packed, and Igor feels proud of his ability to plan things, because even though he’s never been to Cannes before, he had foreseen precisely this situation and reserved a table.","The Winner Stands Alone","Paulo Coelho"},
["16:17"]={"Apparently the great Percy has no sense of humour, for at \003four-seventeen\004 he got tired of it, and hit Skinner crisply in the right eyeball, blacking the same as per illustration.","A Prefect’s Uncle","P.G. Wodehouse"},
["16:18"]={"\0034:18 p.m.\004 Put Toby into his cage","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["16:19"]={"Jessica [\0034:19 PM\004] Don’t tease me like that. I haven’t been to a play in years. Charles [4:19 PM] Then it’ll be my treat. You and the hubby can have big fun on me.","The Other Woman","Eric Jerome Dickey"},
["16:20"]={"\0034:20 p.m.\004 Watch television or a video","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["16:21"]={"\0034:21 pm\004\nAs they started on, Doug picked up a twig and after rubbing it off, started to move one end of it inside his mouth.\n“What are you doing?” Bob asked.\n“Brushing my teeth, nature style,” Doug answered.\nBob grunted, smiling slightly. “I’ll use my toothbrush,” he said.","Hunted Past Reason","Richard Matheson"},
["16:22"]={"Monday, \0034:22 pm\004, Washington, D.C. Paul Hood took his daily late-afternoon look at the list of names on his computer monitor.","Balance of Power: Op-Center 05","Tom Clancy, Steve Pieczenik, and Jeff Rovin"},
["16:23"]={"\00316:23 CET\004\nAfter stowing their bags in the sleeping quarters below, the two new itinerant deckhands reported for duty on the main deck.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["16:24"]={"Mike winked at Ashley and continued with the remaining greetings and hugs and handshakes. The time was \0034:24\004. Six hours to go. The minutes seemed to just melt away.","Teardrop","Travis Thrasher"},
["16:25"]={"He jumped off at St. Paul’s and, although he walked slowly, he was standing outside Kaufman’s bank on Cheapside by \0034:25\004.","Mightier Than the Sword","Jeffrey Archer"},
["16:26"]={"It seemed all wrong to have thought of such a thing. She thought, “I don’t know him. Nor does he know me. Nor ever shall we.” She put her bare hand in the sun, where the wind would weather it. It was \003twenty-six minutes after four\004.","Catch-As-Catch-Can","Charlotte Armstrong"},
["16:27"]={"Still no sign of Juliet. Patricia gave a surreptitious glance at her watch; \003twenty-seven minutes past four\004 — no! nearly twenty-eight past — Oh, hurry up, Juliet, hurry up, do!","Visitors for the Chalet School","Elinor Brent-Dyer"},
["16:28"]={"Same day: \0034:28 pm\004 — Right turn at the second bus stop after the gas station. I stopped the car at the first ward post office and inquired at the corner tobacconists. Mr. M’s house was the one to the right of the post office, visible diagonally in front of me.","The Ruined Map: A Novel","Kobo Abe"},
["16:30"]={"The local police wouldn’t relish being called out at \0034:30\004 on Christmas Eve, and if this was some kind of hoax he preferred not to be an active participant.","The Mistletoe Murder","P.D. James"},
["16:31"]={"From: Renee Greene – August 5, 2011 – \0034:31 PM\004 To: Shelley Manning Subject: Re: All Access What should I be worried about, then? JUST KIDDING. You’re right. Well, I gotta run, my groupie friend. I actually have REAL work to do. I’ll talk to you tonight.","Click: An Online Love Story","Lisa Becker"},
["16:32"]={"\0034:32 pm\004. Now the eight Marines next to us leave their emplacement and file quickly past, the last saying, “Go! Go! Go!” They break into a run.","Seek","Denis Johnson"},
["16:33"]={"At \0034:33\004, the second bus maneuvered its way onto the main thoroughfare, where they were held up by early commuters on their way home from work, while they were on their way to work.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["16:34"]={"A bedroom stocked with all the ordinary, usual things. There was a wardrobe in the corner. A bedside table with a collection of water glasses of varying ages and an alarm clock with red digital numbers — \0034:34 p.m.\004","The Raw Shark Texts","Steven Hall"},
["16:35"]={"The Voice shut itself off with a click, and then reopened conversation by announcing the arrival at Platform 9 of the \0034:35\004 from Birmingham and Wolverhampton.","4:50 from Paddington","Agatha Christie"},
["16:36"]={"They watched their friend through the glass cover; the heaving of the chest became less and less, the breathing lower and lower, while a purple hue settled upon his body. At \003thirty-six minutes past four\004, the last division of the wheel had been reached.","A.D. 2000","Alvarado M. Fuller"},
["16:37"]={"She should have been home by now. \0031637\004. Yes. It’s as if I had the date of a year on my arm. Every day is a piece of world history.","101 Reykjavik","Hallgrímur Helgason"},
["16:38"]={"I let him put me in the car and drive me to the station. At \003twenty-two minutes to five\004 by the clock in the station house I was in front of a cell in the Mill River jail.","At Catskill Eagle","Robert B. Parker"},
["16:39"]={"He looked at the clock on his desk: \0034:39\004. “Get me the checkpoint at Khalis,” he instructed the young Lieutenant.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["16:40"]={"\003Four forty\004 P.M. Besta sang another hymn. Everyone knew something was wrong. How long did they wait? The mayor was going crazy inside, as was the mayor’s wife, as was their daughter. Seiji could barely contain his rage. He was turning as red as his red tuxedo.","Trouble & Triumph: A Novel of Power & Beauty","Tip “T.I.” Harris with David Ritz"},
["16:41"]={"She’d opened the door at \003nineteen minutes to five\004, thinking she had some measure of control over her world. Now she knew it for the lie it was. Everything she once thought she knew was upside-down; everything had changed.","Who Do You Trust","Melissa James"},
["16:42"]={"I’m always happy when I reach the finish line of a long-distance race, but this time it really struck me hard. I pumped my right fist into the air. The time was \0034:42 pm\004. Eleven hours and forty-two minutes since the start of the race.","What I Talk About When I Talk About Running","Haruki Murakami"},
["16:43"]={"The deputies huddled in the lee of the Land Cruiser while Cork briefed them. Oren Esterville had called the sheriff’s office at \0034:43 P.M.\004 to report his wife missing.","Corpus Delicti","William Kent Krueger"},
["16:44"]={"At \003sixteen minutes to five\004 Mr. Beveridge stood by the side of Clankwood Avenue, comfortably wrapped in Dr. Escott’s fur coat, and smoking with the greatest relish one of Dr. Escott’s undeniable cigars.","The Lunatic at Large","J. Storer Clouston"},
["16:45"]={"At \003four-forty-five\004 Miss Haddon went to tea with the Principal, who explained why she desired all the pupils to learn the same duet. It was part of her new co-ordinative system.","Co-ordination","E.M. Forster"},
["16:46"]={"At \0034:46\004 an obese, middle-aged man shuffled in. Wearing a starched guayabera and dark green pants, Ureña asked for a book on confectionery, then took a seat at the end of the same reading room. Evelina and Leticia exchanged astonished glances. It definitely was one of those days.","Havana World Series","José Latour"},
["16:47"]={"But maybe it was more than that, maybe Affenlight had erred badly somehow, because here it was 4:49 by his watch, \0034:47\004 by the wall clock, and Owen had not yet come.","The Art of Fielding","Chad Harbach"},
["16:48"]={"By \003four forty-eight\004 the five-man team had her back again and the urgent struggle to save Ellen’s life continued. She’d now been undergoing surgery for the best part of two hours, and it was doubtful her body could sustain much more trauma.","Taking Chances","Susan Lewis"},
["16:49"]={"\0034:49 p.m.\004, a bald-headed man wearing khakis and ankle-high deck shoes came out through the front door of the purple house on 21st Avenue East. The detectives had nicknamed him the General.","Beyond Recognition","Ridley Pearson"},
["16:50"]={"They had all frozen at the same time, on a snowy night, seven years before, and after that it was always \003ten minutes to five\004 in the castle.","The 13 Clocks","James Thurber"},
["16:51"]={"At \0034:51\004, a figure in a cherry — red parka exits the library, pulls up her hood, and pushes a snow shovel up and down the front walk.","Cloud Cuckoo Land","Anthony Doerr"},
["16:52"]={"The corrida was to begin at five o’clock. The five-footed beasts make a point of arriving at the latest at eight or seven minutes to: ritual again. At \003eight minutes to five\004, there they were. The urchins gave them a tap on the shoulder: another bit of ritual.","Chaos and Night","Henry De Montherlant"},
["16:53"]={"It was so quiet in the post office that Trinidad could hear the soft tick of the clock’s second hand every time it moved. It was now \003seven minutes before five\004.","The Silence of Bonaventure Arrow","Rita Leganski"},
["16:54"]={"At \003six minutes to five\004, he leaned forward and picked up the black phone. He dialed the number of an estate agent in Mayfair, and asked to speak to the senior partner.","Mightier Than the Sword","Jeffrey Archer"},
["16:55"]={"Darkness had fallen. Glancing at the dashboard, she saw that it was \003four-fifty-five\004. She had been on the road for nearly three hours.","The Private Patient","P.D. James"},
["16:56"]={"And when that final Friday came, when my packing was mostly done, she sat with my dad and me on the living-room couch at \0034:56 P.M.\004 and patiently awaited the arrival of the Good-bye to Miles Cavalry.","Looking for Alaska","John Green"},
["16:57"]={"Tom O’Sullivan and Phillip Taylor were kibitzing at the counter of Nikki’s Hot Dog Stand as they placed their order \003shortly before 5:00 p.m.\004","The Ambition","Lee Strobel"},
["16:58"]={"It’s \003nearly five o’clock\004 and the sun has dried the ground so hard that the edges of the lawns are cracked and hard, as threadbare and brown as worn carpet.","The Song Collector","Natasha Solomons"},
["16:59"]={"\003One minute to five\004.\nThe needles flashed silver fire. They swam like a tiny school of metal fish in the darkening summer air.","Embroidery","Ray Bradbury"},
}
